  <event id="29">
      <start>11:00</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>AW1.126</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>The Newcons Project</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>BSD</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Last year I gave a talk on the state of FreeBSD&amp;#39;s console driver called syscons. Since then I&amp;#39;ve started working on a new console driver architecture for the kernel, which I&amp;#39;m hoping will be finished before FreeBSD 9.0.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will describe how the new console driver is implemented and will highlight some of its key features, such as exclusive support for UTF-8 and reduced graphics I/O.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="291">Ed Schouten</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>